armada fleet — the agents you do not talk to: Jobs, Drones, worktrees

VERBS
  spawn <task>           start an isolated agent Job on a task
  ls                     what is running, what it has spent, and who needs you
  show <job>             one Job in full, and why it needs you
  board <job>            take a Job over yourself: worktree and resume command
  answer <job> <answer>  give a waiting Job your decision; let it continue
  inbox                  what the fleet needs from you
  pause <job>            stop a Job's Drone and keep everything else
  resume <job>           start a paused Job's session again
  reap                   end every finished Job and release what they hold
  kill [<job>]           end a Job and release everything it owns

`armada fleet <verb> --help` for one verb's usage and flags.

You ask for work; that is a Job. Something runs it; that is a Drone.

The two are separate so that a crash, a reboot or a killed process
does not lose the work — the Job keeps its branch, its notes and what
it spent, and you can pick it up later with `board`.

Board does not attach. It hands you the conversation to drive yourself, in the
Job's own worktree — Armada owns no terminal.
